class SequentialHyperedge {
  definition {
    An ISO 12620 A.6.3 / ISO 704:2022 §5.5.5 sequential relation
    connecting a comprehensive concept to two or more subordinate
    concepts that are ordered by some criterion of sequencing
    (temporal, spatial, causal, developmental, process-step, etc.).

    Mirror of PartitiveHyperedge and GenericHyperedge. Members are
    ordered (unlike Partitive/Generic where order is insignificant).
    The same comprehensive can have multiple sequential rakes
    distinguished by criterion of subdivision (multidimensionality,
    ISO 704:2022 §5.6.3).

    ISO 12620 A.6.3 subtypes:
      temporal relation   — earlier/later occurrence (cause → effect)
      spatial relation    — relative position in space (floor → ceiling)
      developmental       — step in a process (tadpole → frog)
      causal              — cause → effect (humidity → corrosion)

    Use cases:
      manufacturing process steps
      biological life cycles
      software release lifecycles
      supply chain stages
      geological eras

    Distinct from binary sequentially_related / spatially_related /
    temporally_related edges. A single sequential assertion should
    use the binary edge; a rake of N ordered steps should use
    SequentialHyperedge.
  }
  +comprehensive: <<StandardDocument>> ReferenceToTermbase [1] {
    definition {
      The starting or comprehensive concept of the sequence.
    }
  }
  +members: SequentialMember [2..*] {
    definition {
      Two or more subordinate concepts in the sequence, in the order
      they appear in the sequence.
    }
  }
  +completeness: Completeness [0..1] {
    definition {
      Whether the encoded members constitute the entire sequence
      (complete) or only some of it (partial).
    }
  }
  +criterion: <<BasicDocument>> LocalizedString [0..1] {
    definition {
      The sequencing criterion (temporal order, spatial order, causal
      chain, process step index, etc.). Distinguishes distinct rakes
      on the same comprehensive per ISO 704:2022 §5.6.3.
    }
  }
  +sources: ConceptSource [0..*] {
    definition {
      Bibliographic references for this specific hyperedge.
    }
  }
  +notes: <<BasicDocument>> LocalizedString [0..1] {
    definition {
      Free-form localized commentary.
    }
  }
  +status: ConceptStatus [0..1] {
    definition {
      Lifecycle status, independent of the comprehensive concept's
      status.
    }
  }
}
